Byron A Jeff wrote:

[long and pertinent instruction for AC and protection]

For a while I tried the pure protection rakcet, but being so feeble and
trying to get to minetown result in a *lot* of dead characters. Spiked
pits, starvation, exploding chests, volley of arrows, etc. I think the
strategy is good for VERY careful players and pros.

Regarding AC and XP level I try to balance the two - characters who
have an hard time finding good armor will refrain from getting too much
experience. If I hit negative AC and I'm still low level - it's
protection time!

I always get some protection, but XP level 1 isn't all that important,
especially for characters who have an easy time generating money -
something the archeologist definitely can do. Arcs can identify and
sell gems, everybody can sell found spellbooks and other valuable items
(then steal them back and resell them ad-nauseam), etc.

With archeologist II typically buy my first protection around XP level
4 to 6. It makes it a lot more expensive, but the xtra HP, makes for
easier exploration, more chance to survive traps or a hit from a +2
dwarvish mattock. It's a lot more comfortable searching for the vaults
if you have found all the food from the first 10 or so dungeon levels.
just my 2 cents


